    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "https://www.auctioneera.ie/property/woodside-healys-bridge-kerry-pike-cork-t12-fwp5\r\nImportant note: Details of upcoming viewings and latest offers are available at the Auctioneera website link above.\r\n\r\nAuctioneera is delighted to present Woodside, Healy's Bridge, Kerry Pike in Cork.\r\n\r\nWoodside is a distinctive two-bedroom semi-detached period home offering a blend of original character and practical modern updates. Dating from 1870 and originally built as a station house, the property retains many features reflective of its period origins. Its red-brick façade, contrasting stone detailing, tall arched windows and steep gabled rooflines create an immediately recognisable exterior. The property also benefits from generous on-site parking for up to three cars.\r\n\r\nInside, the generously proportioned living room features exposed original stonework, an arched fireplace with a fitted stove and refurbished original windows incorporating traditional blown glass. These carefully retained details provide a tangible connection to the building's history, while concrete floors throughout offer a practical and durable foundation.\r\n\r\nThe fitted kitchen and dining space combines traditional-style cabinetry, timber worktops, a Belfast sink and ample preparation and storage space. Large windows bring natural light into the room and provide views towards the surrounding greenery. Recent works also include renewed roofing over the kitchen and bathroom portion of the house.\r\n\r\nFrom the kitchen, the accommodation continues into a bright sun lounge with windows on two sides. This versatile room enjoys views of the river and provides direct access to the gravelled riverside terrace.\r\n\r\nThe property offers two bedrooms arranged across two levels. A well-proportioned bedroom with windows on two sides is situated on the ground floor, while the primary bedroom occupies the upper level beneath sloping ceilings and benefits from useful built-in eaves storage. The bathroom is fitted with a shower, wash-hand basin and WC, providing a practical and neatly presented space.\r\n\r\nThe outdoor setting is one of the property's most distinctive features. A broad gravelled terrace extends along the river-facing side of the house, providing space for outdoor seating while enjoying views across the water. Steps lead towards the water's edge, and the property benefits from direct river access and fishing rights. A separate lawned garden, mature trees and a sheltered seating area further enhance the peaceful natural surroundings.\r\n\r\nSituated beside Healy's Bridge in Kerry Pike, Woodside combines a wooded riverside setting with convenient access to Cork city and surrounding amenities. Local schools, shops and sporting facilities are within easy reach, while nearby road connections and local bus services support straightforward commuting.\r\n\r\nWoodside presents a rare opportunity to acquire a manageable home with genuine period character. Its former station-house heritage, preserved original features, mature grounds and exceptional river frontage combine to create a property of real individuality."
      },
